Art union gaming activities
The awarding of prizes by lot by an art union (an art union gaming activity) is a
permitted gaming activity for the purposes of section 10 of the Act if the following
requirements are complied with—


(a) not less than 30% of the gross proceeds of the gaming activity are paid to the
benefiting organisation,

<!-- rtdf-block-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_art_union:b0003; role: provision; provision-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_art_union:p0001; source-lines: 2-9; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```

(b) the total value of all the prizes exceeds $30,000,

<!-- rtdf-block-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_art_union:b0004; role: provision; provision-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_art_union:p0002; source-lines: 10-10; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```

(c) the maximum amount of money payable as a separate prize does not exceed
$30,000,

<!-- rtdf-block-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_art_union:b0005; role: provision; provision-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_art_union:p0003; source-lines: 11-12; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```

(d) the person conducting the activity holds an authority to do so that is in force
and the activity is conducted in accordance with the authority

<!-- rtdf-block-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_art_union:b0006; role: provision; provision-id: NSW_community_gaming/nsw_art_union:p0004; source-lines: 13-14; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```

